{"type":"tool_end","payload":{"toolCallId":"toolu_01GpJZn18ZUwLEiKY5BCANYV","result":"<file path=\"/Users/andres.mesa/.coda/skills/generate-context-pack/references/phase-a-analysis-loading.md\" lines=\"54\" start=\"1\" end=\"54\" returned=\"54\" has_more=\"false\" truncated=\"false\">\n     1|# Phase A — Analysis Loading & Target Selection\n     2|\n     3|## Context Contract\n     4|\n     5|- **H1 Title:** Phase A — Analysis Loading & Target Selection\n     6|- **Inputs:** `INPUT_ANALYSIS/analysis.md` (required); `INPUT_ANALYSIS/meeting-analysis.md` and `INPUT_ANALYSIS/transcripts/*` (optional); `target_files` parameter.\n     7|- **Outputs:** none written in this phase — it populates the in-memory target list and the per-file source map consumed by Phase B.\n     8|- **Carries Forward:** `TARGET_FILES[]` (catalog entries to generate), `SOURCE_MAP` (`filename → analysis.md section(s)`), `EVIDENCE_INDEX` (`filename → has_sufficient_evidence: bool`).\n     9|- **Flush After:** raw `analysis.md` body — Phase B re-reads only the section(s) that feed the file it is currently generating (do not hold the whole analysis in memory across files).\n    10|- **Dependency:** runs after the FIRST ACTION `_progress.json` write (§2) and Memory Bank Session Start (§4); before Phase B.\n    11|- **Used by step:** SKILL.md Step 1.\n    12|\n    13|## Mode-specific behavior\n    14|\n    15|- **BUILD:** load the analysis, select the full catalog (or the `target_files` subset), build `SOURCE_MAP` + `EVIDENCE_INDEX`, hand off to Phase B.\n    16|- **REPAIR (§7):** do NOT reload/rescan the entire analysis. Restrict `TARGET_FILES` to the file(s) named in the `## ⚠️ Repair feedback` block; reuse the existing pack for all other files. Reload only the analysis section(s) feeding the targeted file(s).\n    17|\n    18|## Step A1 — Read the analysis\n    19|\n    20|1. Confirm `INPUT_ANALYSIS/analysis.md` exists. If missing → STOP-GATE (Gap Report + EXIT, §9). This skill never generates a pack without an analysis to trace to.\n    21|2. Read `analysis.md`. If `meeting-analysis.md` is present, read it too — its `## For <file>` sections are additive evidence for the same target files.\n    22|3. If `transcripts/` is present, treat it as supporting evidence only; the structured `## For <file>` sections in the analysis remain the primary source.\n    23|\n    24|## Step A2 — Select the target file set\n    25|\n    26|- `target_files == all` (default) → every entry in `references/file-catalog.md`.\n    27|- `target_files == <comma-separated list>` → only those catalog filenames. Ignore names not in the catalog and note them in the audit.\n    28|- `context-pack-index.md` is always generated last (SKILL.md Step 3) regardless of the subset — it links whatever files were produced.\n    29|\n    30|## Step A3 — Build the source map & evidence index\n    31|\n    32|For each target file, record from `references/file-catalog.md`:\n    33|- `SOURCE_MAP[filename]` = the `analysis.md` section(s) that feed it (the catalog `Source:` line).\n    34|- `EVIDENCE_INDEX[filename]` = whether those sections contain concrete, non-empty evidence.\n    35|\n    36|## Step A4 — Source-fidelity gate (pre-write, per file)\n    37|\n    38|This is the anti-hallucination gate that Phase B enforces before writing each file:\n    39|\n    40|- Every `## Mandatory Rule` a file will contain MUST map to a specific statement in its\n    41|  `SOURCE_MAP` section(s). A rule with no traceable source is a fabrication — drop it.\n    42|- If a file's `SOURCE_MAP` sections are empty or too thin to support any Mandatory Rule,\n    43|  mark `EVIDENCE_INDEX[filename] = insufficient`. Phase B then emits the `[TO BE COMPLETED]`\n    44|  skeleton for that file (mandatory format + `status: pending — insufficient evidence`),\n    45|  **still carrying valid `when_to_read` frontmatter** (the routing hint is independent of\n    46|  body completeness).\n    47|\n    48|## Zero Invention application (this phase)\n    49|\n    50|- Selection and mapping only — invent nothing here.\n    51|- `[INFERRED]` hints are permitted downstream only in `## Recommended Rules` and must be\n    52|  tagged; they never become Mandatory Rules. Phase A simply flags where evidence is thin so\n    53|  Phase B can route to the `[TO BE COMPLETED]` path instead of inventing rules to fill it.\n    54|\n</file>","isError":false}}
