vironment validation successful (source: `architecture/ARCH-SPEC.md` line 103-106).\n   127|- Desktop viewport (1920x1080) is the initial supported compatibility target (NFR-004) (source: `prd.md` line 74-77).\n   128|- Type checking must run as a CI gate separate from the build (origin: blueprint `node-typescript` §6).\n   129|\n   130|### Test Frameworks and Patterns\n   131|status: complete\n   132|- Playwright Test 1.40+ as the test runner (source: `adrs/ADR-SPEC.md` line 44; `architecture/ARCH-SPEC.md` line 85).\n   133|- Page Object Model pattern: element locators, page actions, validation helpers separated per SVC-002 (source: `architecture/ARCH-SPEC.md` line 10-13).\n   134|- Sequential execution for order-dependent tests, parallel execution for independent multi-language tests, retry with exponential backoff for flaky network/timing conditions (source: `architecture/ARCH-SPEC.md` line 51-63).\n   135|- Multi-viewport testing planned: mobile (375px), tablet (768px), large desktop (1440px) (source: `epics.md` EPIC-007, line 107-119).\n   136|- Cross-browser expansion planned (Firefox, Safari, Edge) beyond current Chrome-only implementation (source: `prd.md` FR-005, line 49-55; `epics.md` EPIC-006, line 90-104).\n   137|- SPIKE-001 Selector Strategy Research (dynamic FIFA website content, 2 days), SPIKE-002 Performance Testing Integration (3 days), SPIKE-003 Visual Testing Framework evaluation (2 days) (source: `epics.md` line 139-152).\n   138|\n   139|## For security.md\n   140|### Security Patterns Found\n   141|status: pending - no evidence in inputs\n   142|- None of the four analyzed project inputs (PRD, epics, ADR-SPEC, ARCH-SPEC) describe authentication, authorization, secrets handling, or other security patterns for this project. The project's own assumption is that no authentication is required for the public pages under test (source: `prd.md` ASM-003, line 111-113), which is a scope statement rather than a security pattern.\n   143|- Security controls are supplied entirely by the staged L4 blueprints (origin: blueprint): `security-baseline` states platform-neutral invariants (identity delegation, input validation, secrets management, dependency supply-chain review — `blueprint_id: security-baseline`, §3-§9); `pre-ship-checklist` states verification gates including a dependency audit and secret scan in Gate 0 (`blueprint_id: pre-ship-checklist`, §2).\n   144|\n   145|### Security Gaps or Risks\n   146|status: complete\n   147|- RSK-002 Rate Limiting/Blocking: automated access to the target site may trigger rate limiting or IP blocking; mitigation is test delays and possibly rotating IP addresses (source: `prd.md` line 86-89).\n   148|- RSK-001 Website Structure Changes: FIFA may change website structure, breaking navigation tests; mitigation is robust selectors and regular test maintenance (source: `prd.md` line 81-84).\n   149|- [Blueprint gap, not a project fact] Dependency audit is a required Gate-0 CI check per `pre-ship-checklist` (§2) and `node-typescript` (§8, `pnpm audit --audit-level=high`), but no dependency-audit command or tool is named in any of the four analyzed project inputs — see Open Questions.\n   150|\n   151|## For constraints.md\n   152|### Hard Constraints Found\n   153|status: complete\n   154|- Website `https://inside.fifa.com/` must be available during test execution (ASM-001, high confidence) (source: `prd.md` line 103-105).\n   155|- Test execution environment must have stable internet connectivity (ASM-002, high confidence) (source: `prd.md` line 107-109).\n   156|- Page structure assumed to remain consistent during development phase (ASM-004, medium confidence) (source: `prd.md` line 115-117).\n   157|- Browser-specific configurations must be externalized to support future browser expansion (source: `prd.md` FR-005, line 55).\n   158|- Code coverage must exceed 80% (Gate-001 Code Quality) (source: `architecture/ARCH-SPEC.md` line 97).\n   159|- Tests must pass in CI/CD pipeline and